/* Slider on the native range input:
   <input type="range" class="nui-slider" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="40"
          data-event-change="set_volume(ev.value)"/>
   RmlUi builds the parts (slidertrack, sliderprogress, sliderbar and the arrow
   buttons) as children of the input; the arrows stay 0 wide.

   Where RmlUi 6.3 puts the parts (WidgetSlider.cpp):
   - slidertrack and sliderbar sit at their own margin from the input's top
     edge, so each is centered with margin-top = (20dp - its height) / 2;
   - sliderprogress sits where the track is, plus its own margin, and without
     a height it takes the track's, so it needs neither;
   - the input's own border and padding are not taken into account, so give
     .nui-slider none (nor .nui-focusable).
   is-hover, is-active and is-focus force a state without the pointer or the
   keyboard (gallery snapshots). */

.nui-slider
{
	display: inline-block;
	width: 200dp;
	height: 20dp;
	vertical-align: middle;
}
.nui-slider slidertrack
{
	margin-top: 8dp;
	height: 4dp;
	border-radius: 2dp;
	background-color: var(--surface-sunken);
}
.nui-slider sliderprogress
{
	border-radius: 2dp;
	background-color: var(--accent);
}
.nui-slider sliderbar
{
	margin-top: 2dp;
	box-sizing: border-box;
	width: 16dp;
	height: 16dp;
	border-width: 2dp;
	border-color: var(--accent);
	border-radius: 8dp;
	background-color: var(--surface-raised);
}
.nui-slider sliderbar:hover, .nui-slider sliderbar:active,
.nui-slider.is-hover sliderbar, .nui-slider.is-active sliderbar
{
	background-color: var(--accent);
}
.nui-slider:focus-visible sliderbar, .nui-slider.is-focus sliderbar
{
	border-color: var(--focus-ring);
}
.nui-slider:disabled
{
	opacity: 0.45;
}
